@meeting crossingBackVance
// The ending (E-1, EN2 for lead 39; plans/ending-spec.html, "Crossing back, announced"): Wednesday Day 31 in the
// morning, Commander Vance comes to find you (the Works bay, or wherever you are). Then a notice and his Mail as the
// record. A stand-in for SW6's words (about 7 lines, two replies). They/them for you, or your name. Never "permission"
// or "leave" about the reach: we "cross back over the Line".
title: Crossing back
from: Commander Teo Vance
gist: Commander Vance: Sunday at 14:30 the Wren crosses back over the Line, in the bow lounge. You lead the oath this time.
== lines
vance > you: {me}. A word. Walk with me, or stand still. Either.   [nod]
vance: Sunday at 14:30 the Wren crosses back over the Line. The bow lounge again, the horn again.
vance > you: And this time you'll lead the oath. Basil's the only first-timer. Be gentle. Or don't.
? choice
* I'll be there. I'll learn the words.   rel:vance+1
  vance: You know them already. You heard them four weeks ago.   [nod]
* Me? Why me?   rel:vance+2
  vance: The Captain asked for you by name. I didn't argue. I rarely do.
vance: Clean boots. The punch is Brennan's problem, not yours. As you were.   [nod]
